T3.3 morphology against cv::erode / cv::dilate / cv::morphologyEx on the
REFERENCE DEVICE -- raw log for EXPERIMENTS.md X-13
================================================================================

PLATFORM -- the environment block scripts/run_on_pi.sh printed for this run.
A run with a non-zero throttle flag at either end is INVALID, not merely slow,
so both are recorded here rather than summarised:

  device:           pi4
  cpu:              Raspberry Pi 4 Model B Rev 1.5 (Cortex-A72)
  arch / kernel:    aarch64 / 6.18.34+rpt-rpi-v8
  compiler:         g++ (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0
  build:            Release, -DBINCV_USE_OPENCV=ON (BINCV_PI_OPENCV=1)
  governor:         performance (restored to ondemand on exit)
  core pinning:     taskset -c 3
  throttled before: throttled=0x0
  throttled after:  throttled=0x0
  commit:           f2544ef, PLUS the uncommitted T3.3 tree (see below)

WHAT TREE THIS IS, since the commit field alone does not say. `f2544ef` is HEAD
and it contains none of T3.3's files -- ops/morphology.hpp,
benchmark/morphology_benchmark.cpp and tests/test_morphology.cpp are all still
untracked at the time of this run, so the commit hash does not pin what was
measured. The sources that produced the numbers below are recorded by content,
as bincv-cpp/results/denoise_benchmark_pi4.log established for X-12:

  sha256[0:16]  3a7ca2db51beaf5e  bincv-cpp/include/bincv-cpp/ops/morphology.hpp
  sha256[0:16]  fb6802ea8f489065  bincv-cpp/benchmark/morphology_benchmark.cpp
  sha256[0:16]  9e90a94e35fffc11  bincv-cpp/include/bincv-cpp/ops/shift.hpp
  sha256[0:16]  184c9eb2b732c9f4  bincv-cpp/include/bincv-cpp/ops/logic.hpp
  sha256[0:16]  9b9f473084856fad  bincv-cpp/benchmark/bench_util.hpp

  WHEN T3.3 LANDS, replace the commit line above with the landing commit and
  amend this log into it, as results/logic_benchmark_pi4.log does -- those
  hashes then become checkable against a tracked tree rather than against a
  working directory nobody else has.

COMMAND

  BINCV_PI_OPENCV=1 ./scripts/run_on_pi.sh pi4 \
      './benchmark/morphology_benchmark > morphology_benchmark.log'

  BINCV_PI_OPENCV=1 is not optional: the denominator is an OpenCV call and the
  device's default build is core-only.

REPRODUCIBILITY. Four runs of this benchmark were taken on this device during
T3.3's review. Within one build the 640x480 erode 3x3 uint32 row read 0.72195,
0.73935, 0.72016 and 0.72014 ns/pixel -- 2%. ACROSS builds it moves more than
that: the same library call, timed by benchmark/morphology_path_benchmark.cpp
instead, reads 0.66153 ns/pixel at a 0.1% batch spread. That 9% is the
translation unit's code layout, not the kernel, and it is why the erode 3x3
uint32 row is reported below as a TIE with cv::erode rather than as the 1.11x an
earlier single run was quoted at. See X-13.

